From 01af461c5b8bf3313ab5517ddc240894fc9cc25b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maccn <uuhunter@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 21:32:16 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: support native Windows (MSVC) build
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Make continuwuity compile and run natively on x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
(no WSL/Docker). Build with:

  cargo build --release --no-default-features --features \
    "zstd_compression,brotli_compression,gzip_compression,\
     media_thumbnail,url_preview,ring,element_hacks,\
     bindgen-runtime,release_max_log_level"

(Linux-only features off: io_uring / jemalloc / systemd / journald /
hardened_malloc. RocksDB builds under MSVC unchanged; no fork edits.)

These are conditional-compilation gaps that only surface off-unix; none
change protocol, database, auth, or federation semantics. The set is
atomic — each fix resolves a distinct Windows compile error and only the
full set builds, so they land as one commit to keep the tree buildable.

Fixes:
- media: add cross-platform `symlink_compat()` (unix `fs::symlink`,
  windows `fs::symlink_file`; generic over AsRef<Path>) and route the 4
  legacy-compat-link call sites (mod.rs + migrations.rs x3) through it.
  `tokio::fs::symlink` is unix-only; Windows splits file/dir symlinks.
- admin: keep the `Restart` subcommand variant on all platforms (drop
  its `#[cfg(unix)]`) so the `#[admin_command_dispatch]` proc-macro's
  generated arm is not left dangling (E0422); add a `#[cfg(not(unix))]`
  `restart()` stub returning an error (E0599). In-place re-exec via
  `execvp` stays unix-only.
- router/serve: gate `mod unix;` and the unix-socket branch behind
  `#[cfg(unix)]` (the module is `#![cfg(unix)]`, so `unix::serve` does
  not exist on Windows -> E0433). TLS/plain paths unchanged.
- sys/storage: split `dev_from_path` into a unix impl and a
  `#[cfg(not(target_family="unix"))]` stub returning (0,0). Block-device
  major/minor comes from Linux sysfs; downstream (RocksDB pool auto-tune)
  already tolerates the fallback via `.log_debug_err().unwrap_or_default()`.
- macros/config: propagate a field's `#[cfg(...)]` onto the generated
  `self.#ident` references in the config Display impl, so unix-only
  fields (e.g. `log_to_journald`) don't dangle off-unix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
